{"id":"doc-summary","kind":"document","text":"Executive summary\n\nThe migration moved billing off the legacy cron jobs and onto a single queue. Rollout took three weeks and touched four services. Latency improved by 38% at p95, and the error rate fell to 0.2%. The remaining risk is the retry queue, which still shares a database with the ledger. We recommend splitting it before the next quarter."}
{"id":"doc-readme","kind":"document","text":"## Installation\n\nRun the installer, then start the app from the launcher. The first launch downloads the local model, which takes a few minutes on a slow connection. If the download fails, the app falls back to your configured cloud provider and shows a warning in Settings."}
{"id":"doc-spec","kind":"document","text":"Section 4 — Retention\n\nSnapshots are kept per session only. The transcript is stored locally in the profile file. Nothing leaves the machine unless a cloud provider answers a question, in which case the prompt contains the clipped context packet rather than the raw capture."}
{"id":"doc-abstract","kind":"document","text":"Abstract\n\nWe evaluate endpointing latency across three silence detectors on the same audio set. The state machine dominates the result: switching the per-frame test changes the detected endpoint by less than 40 ms, while the hangover budget moves it by hundreds of milliseconds."}
